{
  "info": {
    "name": "Glonez Backend",
    "description": "Glonez language training centre — Staff + User endpoints, Neero gateway (with anti-spoof callback re-verification), claims, accounts, transfers and withdrawals.\n\nUsage:\n1. Import the matching environment (Development, Staging, or Production).\n2. Run `Staff › Auth › Login` or `User › Auth › Login` — the test script automatically saves `staffToken` / `userToken` to your environment.\n3. All staff/user requests pick up the token via `{{staffToken}}` / `{{userToken}}`.\n\nDev mode (NODE_ENV != production):\nThe backend routes payment & withdrawal calls to an in-process simulator, so use `+237670000001` (the value of `{{devTestPhone}}`) as the phone. Send header `x-simulate-outcome: failed` to force a failed outcome (default = success).\n\nNeero callbacks:\nOne endpoint receives both payment and withdrawal callbacks (`POST /api/public/callbacks/neero`). The server discriminates by the prefix of `externalTransactionId` (`PAY-…` → Payment, `WDR-…` → Withdrawal). PENDING callbacks are acknowledged and ignored. For non-pending callbacks, the server re-queries Neero using the stored `gatewayReference` (the Neero `transactionIntentId`) — the callback body itself never drives the status update, eliminating spoofing.\n\nPagination: list endpoints accept `pageNum` (default 1) and `pageSize` (default 10).\n\nResponse shape: every endpoint returns HTTP 200 with `{ success, data, errorMsg, errorCode }`. Frontends gate on `success` + `errorCode`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "8a3f0a92-glonez-1b3c-4a5d-9e2f-collection01"
  },
